        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat!: replace Code-Hex/vz with a native Swift VM daemon and rename apple-vz to apple-vm",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nRemoves the Code-Hex/vz cgo dependency and renames the provider from `apple-vz` to `apple-vm`.\n\nAll Virtualization.framework work now lives in `crabbox-apple-vm-vmd`, a dependency-free Swift daemon under `vmd/` (VM hosting, EFI/virtio configuration, bounded console log, VSOCK reverse SSH proxy, doctor probe). The Go helper is pure Go (`CGO_ENABLED=0`), embeds the daemon at release build time (`scripts/build-vmd.sh` + `-tags vmdembed`), and installs/entitlement-signs a content-addressed managed copy under the state root itself — so the backend's managed-helper copy/codesign machinery is deleted entirely.\n\n### Why\n\n- Code-Hex/vz was the only cgo dependency; its cgo/ObjC bridge layer (fd lifetimes, dispatch queues, KVO) is exactly the bug class upstream keeps patching. Swift talks to Virtualization.framework natively with no bridge and no third-party code.\n- Same architecture as tart, without the FSL licensing questions (all first-party code).\n- Opens a natural path to macOS guests (`VZMacPlatformConfiguration`) later.\n\n### Rename compatibility\n\nOld names keep working as deprecated aliases:\n\n- provider names `apple-vz` / `applevz` (registered aliases)\n- `appleVZ:` config key (merged when `appleVM:` is absent)\n- `--apple-vz-*` flags and `CRABBOX_APPLE_VZ_*` env vars\n- claim lookups canonicalize stored provider names via the alias registry, so pre-rename leases stay resolvable/cleanable\n- the `state/apple-vz` directory migrates to `state/apple-vm` on first use\n- legacy daemon process-identity checks still recognize `crabbox-apple-vz-helper` processes from older releases\n\n### Protocol notes\n\nThe helper↔daemon contract is unchanged from the old helper↔serve contract: same CLI (`serve --state-root --name --startup-fd`), same startup-authorization byte, same `instance.json` metadata schema (the Swift daemon passes unknown keys through), same kinfo process-identity format, same VSOCK activate/ready channel protocol — the guest cloud-init proxy is untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...` (full suite; two pre-existing flaky controller timing tests pass on rerun), `go test -race` on `internal/applevmhelper`, `internal/providers/applevm`, `internal/providers/all`\n- `npm test --prefix worker`, `node --test scripts/*.test.js` (56/56)\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh` (command surface, provider matrix, links, docs site)\n- Release-style build: `sh scripts/build-vmd.sh && go build -tags vmdembed ./cmd/crabbox-apple-vm-helper`; `vmd-info` reports the embedded payload; daemon minos verified 13.0\n- Live on Apple Silicon (macOS 26): `crabbox doctor --provider apple-vm` fully green (embed extraction → codesign → probe VM creation), and a real end-to-end boot:\n  `crabbox run --provider apple-vm -- uname -a` → downloaded/converted Ubuntu 26.04, booted via the Swift daemon, SSH over the VSOCK reverse proxy, synced the checkout, ran the command (`Linux ... aarch64`), released and cleaned up the lease\n- Codex autoreview: initial run found a release build-tag conflict (`cli_stub.go`) and stale JS release-contract tests — both fixed; re-run clean\n\n## Config/secret implications\n\nNone. No new secrets; entitlement signing remains ad-hoc (`codesign --sign -`) and moves from the backend into the helper. `CRABBOX_APPLE_VM_VMD` is a new optional override for the daemon binary path (source builds).\n",
        "branch": "claude/friendly-proskuriakova-2831a7",
